I'll chime in with my novice experience reading (and particularly
writing) Lojban.

When writing Lojban, I'm inspired to add additional, clarifying details
that I would not add to an English sentence.  This makes my Lojban
longer and presumably more precise.  When speaking with people with
more fluency in Lojban than I have, I've been surprised when they
suggest something to me that I consider too imprecise--I suspect as
my own comfort in Lojban increases the context I'm willing to assume
while writing will tend more toward brevity than it currently does.

-Alan

